; MW1: Critical Hit's House office (src/mw1_office.h), on MW1's screen
; template (src/mw1_screen.h; ANCHOR, LABEL_AT, LABEL_FONT, LABEL_OFF_FONT,
; TEXTS and the _WIDE layout are ours). FIXES.md item 3, CATALOG's 16: the
; office scene, read top to bottom (FIXES.md item 56): REQUEST MISSION (NEXT OFFER once one is up) and LEAVE (BACK)
; at the top of the left column, the House's liaison (named per view, the world's House) under them; the contract on
; offer on the panel, the three terms on the terminal under it, each with MW1's arrows (up asks more, down less, as
; MW1's keys did), and the buttons that act on the terms under the terminal, at its right edge: NEGOTIATE (SUBMIT),
; then ACCEPT, the primary action, framed in amber (MW1's CONTRACT_OFFICE: REQUEST_MISSION_OFFER, NEXT_MISSION_OFFER,
; NEGOTIATE_CONTRACT). The liaison's frame (item 50) as wide as the buttons, edges lined up, a button gap under LEAVE,
; its foot on the button row's; the portrait 4 inside it, cut to fit, never stretched. The plaques: the world and its House; the place
; and the company's funds. All MW1's own art (mw1image.zbd): nothing of
; Pirate's Moon's (FIXES.md item 5; tests/test_mw1_look.cpp).
;
; MW1OFFICEDIALOG is 4:3's (640); MW1OFFICEDIALOG_WIDE the 16:9 canvas's (853).
(
MW1OFFICEDIALOG (
  CURSOR (BITMAP ("mw1_cursor") CENTER (1))
  PRIMITIVES (
    BACKGROUND (POSITION (-107 0) BITMAP ("mw1_office_liaison") ANCHOR ("CENTRE"))
